cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Oct 2026]\nL9: # Title:RealCLI: Toward a Unified Evaluation of Human-Agent Collaboration for CLI Agents\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Yunqi Liu , cite6†Peiyu Wang , cite7†Bingli Wang , cite8†Leo Luo , cite9†Xuanwu Song , cite10†Xudong Ma , cite11†Hongxin Li , cite12†Yaxin Du , cite13†Weicheng Gu , cite14†Fanglin Xu , cite15†Yi Xing , cite16†XiangLong Liu , cite17†Jujie He , cite18†Zhange Zhang , cite19†Huatong Song , cite20†Zhaoyi Li , cite21†Deyang Kong , cite22†Chuan Hao , cite23†Peihao Wu , cite24†Mingjie Tang , cite25†Ran Tao , cite26†Jian Yang , cite27†Wayne Xin Zhao , cite28†Bryan Dai L12: View a PDF of the paper titled RealCLI: Toward a Unified Evaluation of Human-Agent Collaboration for CLI Agents, by Yunqi Liu and 23 other authors\nL13: \nL14: cite29†View PDF cite30†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:Command-line interface (CLI) agents increasingly execute longer-horizon tasks, yet existing benchmarks either assume that user instructions remain fixed throughout execution or evaluate task outcomes without capturing runtime collaboration quality. In this paper, we present REALCLI, a paired benchmark that unifies the evaluation of task execution and human-agent collaboration quality on realistic CLI tasks.\nL16: To comprehensively measure collaboration, REALCLI builds a five-dimensional framework, operationalized into 22 sub-dimensions and 51 interaction scenario templates. REALCLI provides two modes for paired comparison: REALCLI-EXEC supplies complete specifications upfront, whereas REALCLI-COLLAB introduces a scripted user that delivers progressive information, corrections, constraint revisions, and authorization decisions.\nL17: Evaluations reveal profound capability gaps in frontier agents: the best configuration attains an average score of only 49.2%, and when evaluated by the joint collaboration score ($J_{\\mathrm{collab}}$), the peak performance reaches merely 37.6%. These results show that task effectiveness diverges sharply from collaboration quality, with models consistently struggling in steerability, trust calibration, and safety boundary management.\nL18: REALCLI provides a rigorous, reproducible foundation for measuring and advancing collaborative CLI agents.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite31†arXiv:2610.22507 [cs.CL]\nL21:    | (or cite32†arXiv:2610.22507v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL22:    | cite33†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.22507†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Jian Yang [cite34†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:03:13 UTC (1,243 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled RealCLI: Toward a Unified Evaluation of Human-Agent Collaboration for CLI Agents, by Yunqi Liu and 23 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite29†View PDF L35:   * cite30†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite35†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite36†view license L39: \nL40: ### Additional Features\nL41: \nL42:   * cite37†Audio Summary L43: ### Current browse context:\nL44: \nL45: cs.CL\nL46: \nL47: cite38†< prev |   cite39†next > L48: \nL49: cite40†new | cite41†recent | cite42†2026-10 L50: \nL51: Change to browse by:\nL52: \nL53: cite43†cs L54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * cite44†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L58:   * cite45†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L59:   * cite46†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L60: \nL61: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL62: \nL63: ## BibTeX formatted cit